# Per-project Dockerfile customisation hook (Spec 008 FR-008)
#
# THIS FILE IS A PLACEHOLDER. Spec 008 v1 does NOT consume it.
#
# Intended future contract:
#   - `asdd new <id>` copies this file into the new project's workspace as
#     `<workspace>/Dockerfile.project.extras`.
#   - Any entry-point that triggers an image build (`asdd open`, `asdd claude`,
#     `asdd dispatch`, `asdd serve`) detects that the file is non-empty (has at
#     least one non-comment, non-blank line) and, if so, builds a per-project
#     image `asdd/project-<id>:latest` layered on the shared base, using this
#     file as the appended fragment.
#   - If the file is empty (just this header), those commands use the shared
#     base `asdd/project:latest` directly with no per-project build.
#
# Until that machinery lands, editing this file has no effect.
#
# Example future content (do NOT uncomment until the consumer ships):
#   # ARG BASE_IMAGE
#   # FROM $BASE_IMAGE
#   # RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
#   #     dotnet-sdk-9.0 mono-complete \
#   #  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
